# Documentation Discipline

For every code or configuration change, review whether documentation must also change.

Update documentation when changes affect:

- app behavior
- architecture
- public interfaces
- data models
- project setup
- environment variables
- workflows
- GIS/source-layer assumptions
- finding/review/report behavior
- known constraints or limitations
- roadmap/current-state status

Prefer updating documentation in the same task as the code change.

At minimum, review:

- README.md
- AGENTS.md
- docs/CURRENT_STATE.md
- docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
- docs/DATA_SOURCES.md
- docs/REVIEW_POLICY.md
- docs/DECISIONS.md
- docs/ROADMAP.md
- docs/OVERALL_CONTEXT.md

If a code change does not require a documentation update, state that explicitly in the final summary.

Never make behavior-changing code edits while leaving directly related documentation stale.